---
// What the library is, the SRD attribution, and licenses (SPEC.md §9.2, §11).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO_URL } from '../../../lib/site.ts';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base
  title="About · TTRPG Content Library"
  og={{ title: 'About the TTRPG Content Library', description: 'What the library is, where its rules come from, and how it is licensed.' }}
>
  <article class="measure about">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      The TTRPG Content Library is a growing collection of original tabletop
      roleplaying content (creatures, magic items, and spells) built on the
      System Reference Document 5.2 for the 2024 edition of the fifth-edition
      rules. Every entry is stored as data, so its stat block is computed from
      the same rules everywhere it appears. Browse it from the <a href={url()}>gallery</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>SRD attribution</h2>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        This work includes material from the System Reference Document 5.2
        ("SRD 5.2") by Wizards of the Coast LLC, available at <a href="https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd">https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd</a>.
        The SRD 5.2 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
        International License, available at <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode">https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode</a>.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      The library uses only SRD material. It is not affiliated with or
      endorsed by Wizards of the Coast.
    </p>

    <h2>Licenses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Content</strong> (the entries and the generation guidelines): <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Code:</strong> MIT.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fonts:</strong> Alegreya, Alegreya SC, and Alegreya Sans, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Icons:</strong> Lucide, under the ISC License.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Full credits are in <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md`}>ATTRIBUTION.md</a>.
      The source is on <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .about > * + * {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
    }

    .about blockquote {
      border-inline-start: var(--border-width-strong) solid var(--color-border);
      padding-inline-start: var(--space-s);
    }

    .about ul {
      padding-inline-start: var(--space-m);
    }
  }
</style>
